{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VJbMcVan4cG78rgmfeJ1E4","type":"tool_result","content":"=== README.md ===\n     1\t# certbot_renewal\n     2\t\n     3\tRequests and renews Let's Encrypt certificates.\n     4\t\n     5\t## Role variables\n     6\t\n     7\t| Variable | Default | Purpose |\n     8\t|----------|---------|---------|\n     9\t| `certbot_domains` | `[]` | Domains to request certificates for. |\n    10\t| `certbot_email` | `admin@example.com` | Registration contact address. |\n    11\t| `certbot_renew_hour` | `3` | Hour the renewal timer fires. |\n\n=== defaults/main.yml ===\n     1\t---\n     2\tcertbot_domains: []\n     3\tcertbot_email: admin@example.com\n     4\tcertbot_renew_hour: 3\n\n=== tasks/main.yml ===\n     1\t---\n     2\t- name: Install certbot\n     3\t  ansible.builtin.package:\n     4\t    name: certbot\n     5\t    state: present\n     6\t\n     7\t- shell: certbot certificates | grep -c \"VALID\"\n     8\t  register: certbot_valid_count\n     9\t\n    10\t- name: Request a certificate for each domain\n    11\t  ansible.builtin.command: certbot certonly --standalone -d {{ item }} -m {{ certbot_email }} --agree-tos -n\n    12\t  loop: \"{{ certbot_domains }}\"\n    13\t  notify: Reload nginx\n    14\t\n    15\t- name: Write the renewal timer\n    16\t  ansible.builtin.copy:\n    17\t    content: |\n    18\t      [Unit]\n    19\t      Description=Renew certificates\n    20\t      [Timer]\n    21\t      OnCalendar=*-*-* {{ certbot_renew_hour }}:00:00\n    22\t    dest: /etc/systemd/system/certbot-renew.timer\n\n=== handlers/main.yml ===\n     1\t---\n     2\t- name: Reload nginx\n     3\t  ansible.builtin.service:\n     4\t    name: nginx\n     5\t    state: reloaded\n\n=== meta/main.yml ===\n     1\t---\n     2\tgalaxy_info:\n     3\t  role_name: certbot_renewal\n     4\t  author: platform\n     5\t  description: Requests and renews Let's Encrypt certificates.\n     6\t  license: MIT\n     7\t  min_ansible_version: \"2.15\"\n     8\t  platforms:\n     9\t    - name: Debian\n    10\t      versions:\n    11\t        - bookworm\n    12\t  galaxy_tags:\n    13\t    - tls\n    14\tdependencies: []","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"016ef115-af91-4d02-83d9-729bb46b5435","uuid":"ac5070f8-49c3-4001-b01c-e78cfdfdf9c6","timestamp":"2026-09-13T23:13:22.750Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== README.md ===\n     1\t# certbot_renewal\n     2\t\n     3\tRequests and renews Let's Encrypt certificates.\n     4\t\n     5\t## Role variables\n     6\t\n     7\t| Variable | Default | Purpose |\n     8\t|----------|---------|---------|\n     9\t| `certbot_domains` | `[]` | Domains to request certificates for. |\n    10\t| `certbot_email` | `admin@example.com` | Registration contact address. |\n    11\t| `certbot_renew_hour` | `3` | Hour the renewal timer fires. |\n\n=== defaults/main.yml ===\n     1\t---\n     2\tcertbot_domains: []\n     3\tcertbot_email: admin@example.com\n     4\tcertbot_renew_hour: 3\n\n=== tasks/main.yml ===\n     1\t---\n     2\t- name: Install certbot\n     3\t  ansible.builtin.package:\n     4\t    name: certbot\n     5\t    state: present\n     6\t\n     7\t- shell: certbot certificates | grep -c \"VALID\"\n     8\t  register: certbot_valid_count\n     9\t\n    10\t- name: Request a certificate for each domain\n    11\t  ansible.builtin.command: certbot certonly --standalone -d {{ item }} -m {{ certbot_email }} --agree-tos -n\n    12\t  loop: \"{{ certbot_domains }}\"\n    13\t  notify: Reload nginx\n    14\t\n    15\t- name: Write the renewal timer\n    16\t  ansible.builtin.copy:\n    17\t    content: |\n    18\t      [Unit]\n    19\t      Description=Renew certificates\n    20\t      [Timer]\n    21\t      OnCalendar=*-*-* {{ certbot_renew_hour }}:00:00\n    22\t    dest: /etc/systemd/system/certbot-renew.timer\n\n=== handlers/main.yml ===\n     1\t---\n     2\t- name: Reload nginx\n     3\t  ansible.builtin.service:\n     4\t